FINAL ANSWER:
Ownership is spread across many people, so losing one or two would not hurt. The risk is that almost nobody who wrote this code is still around.

I ran `git blame` on every tracked `.go` file except `vendor/` and `zz_generated_flags.go`. The tool's default line counts credit Sam Okafor with 1,631 lines, mostly vendored `x/sys` and `x/term` plus the generated file, so I left those out. That leaves 12,194 live lines from 79 authors.

| Author | Lines | Share | Cumulative | Last commit |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Eric Paris | 2020 | 16.6% | 16.6% | 2018 |
| Alex Ogier | 1237 | 10.1% | 26.7% | 2015 |
| Noah Dietz | 1228 | 10.1% | 36.8% | 2018 |
| Jonathan Reyna | 1044 | 8.6% | 45.3% | 2017 |
| Tamal Saha | 624 | 5.1% | 50.5% | 2018 |
| Riobard | 538 | 4.4% | 54.9% | 2014 |
| therealmitchconnors | 522 | 4.3% | 59.2% | 2019 |
| Georges Varouchas | 454 | 3.7% | 62.9% | 2025 |

(The "Last commit" column comes from the `knowledge_risk` output. Georges Varouchas is the only author in the top eight who has committed since 2019.)

- **Concentration:** The largest author owns 16.6% of live lines, and it takes five people to pass 50%. `bus_factor` agrees: 8 authors cover over 50% of non-merge commits, and it found no directory where one author made more than 80% of the commits. Losing one or two people would remove at most about 27% of the lines.
- **Who wrote the core:** Eric Paris and Alex Ogier wrote most of `flag.go`, `flag_test.go` and the README. Albert Nigmatzianov is the third main author of `flag.go`.
- **Who wrote the typed slice and map files:** Reyna wrote the bool, ip, uint and similar slice files. Dietz wrote the int32, int64, float32 and float64 slices. Saha wrote the `string_to_*` map types. Per-file owners are in the `knowledge_risk` output.
- **Orphaned files:** The tool flags all 93 files as orphaned. That flag is not useful here, because its "inactive" cutoff is 6 months back from today (2026-04-22) and the last commit in the repo is 2026-04-08. Every author counts as inactive, including the recent committers.
- **Who is actually around:** Authors with commits since May 2025 are Tomas Aschan (9), Sebastiaan van Stijn (4), Georges Varouchas (4), Sam Okafor (3), Maximilian Frank (3), and a handful with one commit each. Aschan is the most active reviewer-level contributor. Only Varouchas, with 454 lines, owns much surviving code among them.
- **Small recent owners:** Lena Voss owns `flagset_helpers.go` (93% of it, 133 lines), added in March 2026.
- **Generated code:** `zz_generated_flags.go` is generated by `hack/genflags`, so whoever understands the generator owns it. Sam Okafor committed it, and I did not check who wrote the generator.

As the reviewer, you would be the main person who understands the whole codebase. Commit rate is also low: 1–3 commits a month since January 2026, none in November or December 2025. The practical risk is that nobody can answer "why was this designed this way" for the older code, not that one departure would break anything.

I can go through the history of `flag.go` or the generated-flags change if that helps you start.

